 ============================================
   ATTRIBUTE SELECTOR
   ============================================

   The attribute selector in CSS allows you to select and style
   HTML elements based on attributes and their values,
   without adding extra classes or IDs.

   It is very powerful when you want specific targeting 
   based on HTML attributes.

   Example:
   [attribute]          → selects elements that have the attribute
   [attribute="value"]  → selects elements with exact value
   [attribute^="val"]   → value starts with
   [attribute$="val"]   → value ends with
   [attribute*="val"]   → value contains

   Why use it?
   - Helps target specific elements WITHOUT adding 
     new classes or IDs.
   - Useful for forms, links, images, state-based elements, etc.
